Analyze this {language} code for crash bugs and correctness issues.

Source file:
{source}

Already reported by mechanical pattern analysis — do NOT report these again:
{known_findings}

Detect:
- Null/nil dereference (accessing property on potentially null value)
- Array/slice out-of-bounds access without length check
- Division by zero (dividing by a variable without zero guard)
- Type coercion errors (invalid casts, type assertion without ok check)
- Unhandled error returns that cause nil pointer dereference
- Integer overflow in arithmetic operations
- Stack overflow from unbounded recursion

Return a JSON array of findings. Each finding:
{{
  "bug_type": "NULL_DEREF|BOUNDS|DIV_ZERO|TYPE_ERROR|UNHANDLED_ERROR|OVERFLOW|RECURSION|OTHER",
  "line": <line number>,
  "severity": "high|medium|low",
  "description": "one sentence describing the specific crash scenario",
  "fix": "concrete fix suggestion"
}}

Return [] if no issues found. Return ONLY the JSON array, no prose.
